🚽 math.brainrot — the arithmetic stdrot doesn't have.
🚽
🚽 stdrot is yapping/yappin/baka/ragequit/chill/slorp/bet. There is no rand,
🚽 no sqrt, no floor, no abs, no min/max. Everything the game needs lives
🚽 here, in pure Brainrot, over scalars only.

🚽 Park-Miller "minimal standard" PRNG via Schrage's method.
🚽
🚽 The obvious LCG (s * 1103515245 + 12345) overflows int32, and the
🚽 interpreter is built with -fsanitize=undefined, so that aborts the run
🚽 rather than wrapping. Schrage's factorisation never leaves int32 by
🚽 construction: 16807 * lo with lo < 127773 tops out at 2,147,469,111,
🚽 just under 2^31.
🚽
🚽 Period 2^31-2. Valid seeds are 1 .. 2147483646; 0 is a fixed point.
rizz rng_next(rizz s) {
    rizz hi = s / 127773;
    rizz lo = s % 127773;
    rizz v = 16807 * lo - 2836 * hi;
    edgy (v < 0) { v = v + 2147483647; }
    bussin v;
}

🚽 A seed mapped to roughly 0.0 .. 1.0. Used for spawn jitter.
chad rng_unit(rizz s) {
    bussin (s % 10000) / 10000.0;
}

🚽 A seed mapped to -1.0 .. 1.0.
chad rng_signed(rizz s) {
    bussin ((s % 20000) / 10000.0) - 1.0;
}

chad clampf(chad v, chad lo, chad hi) {
    edgy (v < lo) { bussin lo; }
    edgy (v > hi) { bussin hi; }
    bussin v;
}

chad maxf(chad a, chad b) {
    edgy (a > b) { bussin a; }
    bussin b;
}

chad minf(chad a, chad b) {
    edgy (a < b) { bussin a; }
    bussin b;
}

chad absf(chad v) {
    edgy (v < 0.0) { bussin -v; }
    bussin v;
}

chad lerpf(chad a, chad b, chad t) {
    bussin a + (b - a) * t;
}
